shader: depth-compare texture descriptors stay float on an integer format

From MythosOfs/Orchid 052478de5b. A depth-compare sample (OpImageSampleDref*) needs a float
sampled type, but the texture pass took the type from the TIC format. A TIC entry read past
tic_limit gave a garbage R16G16_UINT, so the fragment shader got a u32 depth image. Mesa's
vtn_handle_texture refuses that with vtn_fail, spirv_to_nir returns NULL and radv_shader_spirv_to_nir
faults at 0x40 on nir->info.internal. Run37 crashed on that instruction; which module the parser
refused there is not known, but this is the one Orchid found in the same game.

diff --git a/src/shader_recompiler/ir_opt/texture_pass.cpp b/src/shader_recompiler/ir_opt/texture_pass.cpp
index ec10da965c..5aaafb71e7 100644
--- a/src/shader_recompiler/ir_opt/texture_pass.cpp
+++ b/src/shader_recompiler/ir_opt/texture_pass.cpp
@@ -1330,7 +1330,10 @@ void TexturePass(Environment& env, IR::Program& program, const HostTranslateInfo
                 });
             } else {
                 count = std::min(count, sampled_dynamic_cap);
-                const bool is_integer{is_texture_pixel_format_integer(cbuf)};
+                // A depth-compare image is float in SPIR-V (OpImageSampleDref* returns a float
+                // and needs a float sampled type). An integer format bound to one is a stale or
+                // out-of-range TIC entry, and the integer type made RADV's spirv_to_nir fail.
+                const bool is_integer{!flags.is_depth && is_texture_pixel_format_integer(cbuf)};
                 index = descriptors.Add(TextureDescriptor{
                     .type = flags.type,
                     .is_depth = flags.is_depth != 0,
